# Ground truth for SYSTEM-LEVEL evaluation of the littering event detector.
#
# Copy this file to data/ground_truth.csv and add one row per test video
# placed in data/test_videos/. Then run:
#
#     python scripts/evaluate.py --model ml/weights/best.pt --waste-classes trash
#
# Columns (order is free; matched by header name; extra columns are ignored):
#   video             file name inside data/test_videos/            [required]
#   expected_incidents 1 = a littering event SHOULD fire,           [required]
#                      0 = NO event should fire
#   scenario          short label shown in the report table         [optional]
#   event_time_s      seconds into the clip when the drop happens;   [optional]
#                     enables the detection-delay metric on true-positive clips
#   notes             free text for your own reference (ignored)     [optional]
#
# Lines starting with '#' and blank lines are ignored. Aim for a balanced set
# (see data/test_videos/README.md): roughly half positive (expected 1) and
# half negative (expected 0), covering the scenarios below.
video,expected_incidents,scenario,event_time_s,notes
drop_and_leave_01.mp4,1,drop+leave,4.5,person sets a bottle down and walks away
drop_and_leave_02.mp4,1,drop+leave,6.2,person tosses a cup and leaves the frame
drop_and_leave_03.mp4,1,drop+leave,,drop time not labelled (delay not measured)
walk_past_litter_01.mp4,0,walk-past,,litter already on the ground before the clip starts
walk_past_litter_02.mp4,0,walk-past,,person walks near pre-existing trash but drops nothing
carry_and_keep_01.mp4,0,carry+keep,,person carries a bottle the whole clip and keeps it
crowd_no_drop_01.mp4,0,crowd,,several people, nobody litters
person_only_01.mp4,0,person-only,,people present, no waste objects at all
